      "section": "Child Development and Pedagogy",
      "subject": "Kohlberg's Moral Development",
      "question_en": "A student decides to obey classroom rules because they fear being reprimanded and losing recess time. According to Lawrence Kohlberg, this represents Pre-conventional Stage 1 (Punishment-Obedience).",
      "question_hi": "एक छात्र कक्षा के नियमों का पालन इसलिए करता है क्योंकि उसे दंडित किए जाने और खेल का समय खोने का डर है। लॉरेंस कोहलबर्ग के अनुसार यह पूर्व-पारंपरिक (दंड और आज्ञाकारिता) को दर्शाता है।",
      "options": [
        "Pre-conventional (Punishment-Obedience)",
        "Conventional (Interpersonal Accord)",
        "Conventional (Law and Order)",
        "Post-conventional (Universal Ethics)"
      ],
      "ans": 0,
      "explanation": "Kohlberg's moral reasoning evolves from external punishment (Pre-conventional) to social conformity (Conventional) to autonomous universal ethics (Post-conventional)."
